From: Garrett Gonzalez-Rivas <emailforggr@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tools/include: define __u128/__s128 for the tools build

Linux 7.3 UAPI headers (shipped by glibc-dev in nixpkgs) use __u128 in
arm64 <asm/ptrace.h> and <asm/sigcontext.h>. Building tools/bpf/resolve_btfids
against a 7.2 tree pulls those system headers in through tools/include,
whose <linux/types.h> shadows the system one and never defines __u128,
so libbpf fails with "unknown type name '__u128'".

Define the types the same way the 7.3 UAPI <linux/types.h> does. An
identical typedef repeated in C11 is accepted, so this is harmless when
the system header also defines them.

---
 tools/include/linux/types.h | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/tools/include/linux/types.h
+++ b/tools/include/linux/types.h
@@ -13,6 +13,11 @@
 #include <asm/types.h>
 #include <asm/posix_types.h>
 
+#ifdef __SIZEOF_INT128__
+typedef __signed__ __int128 __s128 __attribute__((aligned(16)));
+typedef unsigned __int128 __u128 __attribute__((aligned(16)));
+#endif
+
 struct page;
 struct kmem_cache;
 
